133 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (Coca-Cola reported Q4 2025 net revenues of $11.8 billion, up 2% year-over-year. On the bottom line, Q4 EPS grew 4% to $0.53, while comparable \(non-GAAP\) EPS rose 6% to $0.58. A notable detail was a non-cash impairment charge of $960 million tied to the BODYARMOR trademark, which weighed heavily on reported operating income for the quarter. )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [32]
>>
endobj
134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (For the full year, net revenues reached $47.9 billion, up 2%, and comparable for a full-year comparable EPS of $3.00, up 4%. Additionally, currency was a persistent pulling factor throughout the year, with an 8-point currency headwind impacting full-year reported EPS.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [33]
>>
endobj
135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E (On a volume and operational basis, results were mixed but resilient. Global unit case volume grew 1% in Q4, led by Brazil, the United States, and Japan, while full-year volume was flat as growth in Central Asia and North Africa was offset by declines in Mexico and Thailand. A standout was Coca-Cola Zero Sugar, which grew 13% in Q4 and 14% for the full year, with gains across all geographic segments.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [34]
>>
endobj
